{"t": 185.813, "n": 76, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "I marked all six unmarked rows of phase 3 (3.1, 3.2, 3.4, 3.8, 3.9 and 3.10) as done on 2026-11-26. I changed no source or test file in this visit.\n\nTheir files (`regeneration.py`, `__init__.py`, `blueprint.json`, `test_regeneration.py` and `test_regeneration_run.py`) were already in place from earlier visits. Earlier visits marked rows 3.3, 3.5, 3.6, 3.7 and 3.11, and I left those marks alone.\n\nI ran `tests/test_regeneration.py` and `tests/test_regeneration_run.py` from `plugins/temperspec-tgraph`. The background run reported exit code 0. I never read the final pass count, because my read of the output file was denied. The partial output showed 31 dots and no failures.\n\n`regeneration.py` still has the older form of `regeneration_check`. Phase 7 rows 7.1 and 7.10 change that check, and they will rewrite the finding assertions in `test_regeneration.py`.\n\nARTIFACT phase_note: Marked rows 3.1, 3.2, 3.4, 3.8, 3.9 and 3.10; I changed no source or test file because the earlier visits' files already held every row's change. Ran plugins/temperspec-tgraph tests/test_regeneration.py and tests/test_regeneration_run.py: the background run exited 0, and I never read the final pass count (a read of its output file was denied; partial output showed 31 passes, no failures). Did not run test_regeneration_declaration.py (it belongs to row 3.5, which was already marked). Deviations: none. No spec made false that I saw; phase 7 still changes regeneration_check.", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "b2669f12-626c-4351-ad7b-aa6757c39094"}
